WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:07.440
Abdul Aziz Balagaban has been a Muslim rebel
for half his life.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:12.650
For him, like for so many other men in this
part of the country, not becoming a fighter

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:17.150
was never an option.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:22.199
I joined the rebels because of my religion
but it’s more than that.

00:00:22.199 --> 00:00:27.050
I also saw the injustices and the oppression
against my community.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:33.230
That’s why I decided to join.

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:39.010
He and his comrades are part of an armed struggle
between Muslim insurgents and the Philippine

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:43.920
army that has marred this part of the country
for 50 years.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:52.489
As in in many areas of southern Mindanao,
here in the village of Tukanalipao, the majority

00:00:52.489 --> 00:01:02.489
of the population is Muslim - in a country
that otherwise is almost completely catholic.

00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:05.860
The main reason for the conflict is oppression.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:09.950
We’re defending our rights, our land.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:16.770
We feel that we’re being occupied by outsiders,
nothing is ours, they’re taking away what’s

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:19.370
ours and they’re not giving it back.

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:21.270
We always lose out.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:28.290
This is our home and we have nothing.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:34.940
Now many here have real hope that could finally
change.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:41.030
In a referendum the people of Muslim Mindanao
are voting to ratify a law that would grant

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:44.360
them more autonomy.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:50.560
In return, the rebels have to give up their
fight.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:54.390
Like these two gentlemen here, many of the
rebels in this camp have been fighters all

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:55.390
their lives.

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:58.310
Often, it’s the only thing they learned
how to do.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:02.100
But if the autonomy law is ratified, they’ll
have to take off their uniforms, lay down

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:06.320
their arms, and start a new life as civilians.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:09.750
The deal has been in the making for ((more
than two?)) decades.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:13.930
But in the end it took this man to make it
happen.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:19.240
Internationally, President Rodrigo Duterte
is notorious for his draconian war on drugs

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.590
and his verbal outbreaks.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:30.340
But he has been pushing hard for enhanced
autonomy for the country’s Muslims.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:37.380
To many here in Mindanao he is a beacon of
hope.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.030
We take him by his word.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:40.380
We trust him.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:44.890
On television we see how he handles the drug
problem in the Philippines.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:48.270
Offenders are either killed or in prison.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:54.930
That shows that he really means what he says.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:58.430
But success is not only in the hands of the
President.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:03.540
The new law foresees that Muslim Mindanao
will be governed by the rebel leadership.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:09.690
But feuds between powerful family clans, rampant
corruption, and islamic terrorist groups could

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:14.640
undermine the fragile peace deal.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:20.730
A peace many of Abdul’s comrades have sacrificed
their lives for.

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:26.640
I don’t want my children to experience what
I’ve been through.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.360
All I want is for them is to get a good education.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:31.160
I want them to learn to read and write.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:34.330
For fighters like me there is only violence
and war.

00:03:34.330 --> 00:05:03.000
I want my children to live in peace, I want

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:25.540
them

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:29.520
to have peaceful future.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:06:23.680
But Abdul is 
also wary.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:37.990
If

00:06:37.990 --> 00:07:20.270
the agreement fails, he says, everyone here
is ready to go back

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:40.820
to war.

